# Cubeless day-to-sunset transition

The current RX preview previously changed its palette from day to sunset in only
45 game minutes, from 17:00 to 17:45. The level's `RXSkySystem` actor now starts
this transition at 16:00 and takes 1.75 hours, reaching the same sunset endpoint.
Existing RX interpolation carries clouds, direct/ambient lighting, sky and fog
together rather than letting cloud colour drift away from the environment.

Only the preview actor's `SunsetStart`, `SunsetTransition` and review `TimeOfDay`
were saved. The editor is left at 17:00 for review. Textures, cloud shader, colour
palette values, blueprint defaults, source VDB layout and other maps are unchanged.
No rebake or added rendering work is required.

Screenshots were inspected at 16:00, 16:30, 17:00, 17:22:30 and 17:45.
Live cloud-MID colour parameters were sampled every 3.75 game minutes; the
day (12:00), full sunset (17:45), evening (20:00) and midnight colour endpoints
match the previous settings exactly. Direction readbacks from the rapid sample
loop are excluded from that equality claim because component updates may lag;
the solar orbit parameters were not edited.

Verification evidence: complete frozen-input offline full profile, native cold
load with UnrealMCP disabled, and affected-map cook. These checks do not claim a
full-game packaged playtest. Source-map identity and final preview asset hashes
are recorded with the evidence.

